#Rigid rotations and translations of the molecule (DCBPS) are expressed in
#two different ways: as movements around and along the crystallographic axes
#(R_x_1...R_z_2 and T_x_1...T_z_1) or through nine normal modes (R_a1_1...R_y_2_nm)
#and T_a2_1...T_y_2_nm). The rotation R_y_2_nm and the translation T_y_2_nm are
#around and along the b-axis but are independent, in the sense that they
#do not belong to the same Fourier series, of T_y_1, T_y_2 and R_y_1. Therefore
#they need a different (but trivial) transformation matrix.

